  "title": "## Brett said (verbatim) \"Yeah, any running build that's run that should get picked up right away, …",
  "asked": "## Brett said (verbatim) \"Yeah, any running build that's run that should get picked up right away, the queue should stay, everything should stay. It should get picked up. When it comes back on.\" Earlier: \"the console has to recognize there's no active connection and then connect to the next one without AI.\" \"After this account runs out, go to the API ... step number five.\" ## Do now (first) Relaunch every headless build that stopped because of a Claude limit or dead login (log ends with \"You've hit your 5-hour limit\", \"weekly limit\", \"OAuth session expired\" or \"Not logged in\") from where it stopped, on the active account (account-2). Use the builds store + each build's To carry on block; respect agent-slots caps. Keep the queue and order exactly as they are; drop nothing. ## Then build (plain script, zero AI tokens) 1. Watcher (cron or the console server) that reads headless build logs / launch results for those limit/login lines. 2. On a hit: mark that account out (with its reset time from the line), switch the active account to the next saved one in priority order via the existing claude-accounts / ai-keys switch logic; account-5 (API key) is always last. 3. Requeue the stopped build so it resumes by itself on the new account; nothing is lost. 4. When an account's reset time passes, mark it available again and resume any builds still waiting. 5. No veto wait for these automatic switches (it's a script, not a session). Log every switch + a banner line. Tests, report `_claude/builds/reports/resume-and-failover.md`, THREADS row, PR through the merge queue. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
